// What a Khayyam-written compiler needs third: an instance it made itself. The
// language states that declaring a variable does not say how the capsule is
// created or initialized — "creation and initialization remain responsibilities
// of capsule behavior" (docs/khayyam/variable.md → Overview) — and a method body
// can only call methods, declare variables, declare scopes, and return, so what
// a body does to satisfy that responsibility is the question.
//
// The language's position: no literal, no operator, and no construction form
// (docs/khayyam/khayyam.md → Separation of Syntax and Governance, A Principle:
// a bare numeric literal 41 may not appear as a value without a named capsule).

tp Count cp {
}

tp Holder cp {
}

tp Fresh mt (self Holder) (count Count) () {
    vr made Count
    self.Make()(made)
    self.Fill(made)()
}

tp Make mt (self Holder) () (made Count)

tp Fill mt (self Holder) (count Count) ()
